Step 1: Initial Analysis

    Used exiftool to examine the image.jpg metadata

    Discovered a Comment field containing a long hexadecimal string

    Noted the image uses Huffman coding (standard JPEG encoding)

Step 2: Hex String Identification

    The hex string began with 2d2d2d2d2d which translates to "-----" in ASCII

    This pattern indicates a PEM-format private key header

    The complete hex string represented an entire private key file

Step 3: Hex to PEM Conversion

    Saved the hex string to a file

    Converted the hex dump back to binary format using hex decoding

    The resulting file was identified as an OpenSSH private key (no password)

Step 4: Key Verification

    Examined the recovered private key using OpenSSL

    Confirmed it was a valid 2048-bit RSA private key containing:

        Modulus (n)

        Public exponent (e = 65537)

        Private exponent (d)

        Prime factors (p and q)

        Other RSA components

Step 5: Locate Encrypted Flag

    Listed directory contents

    Identified flag.enc as the encrypted message file (256 bytes, matching RSA key size)

Step 6: Decryption

    Used the recovered private key to decrypt flag.enc

    Applied RSA decryption with appropriate padding

Step 7: Retrieve Flag

    Viewed the decrypted output

    Obtained the plaintext flag
